<!DOCTYPE html><html data-dpl-id="dpl_7bRkYCGhasXtZ4VP8hzM1mjwScRh" lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3lg58otdl8my-.css" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ddg70z30qn04.js"/><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/41b5e_o-w2xun.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1cmnso0jnkwt6.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/2-k_577svdq9-.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/turbopack-2l6qdc9b47pt9.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><title>Run the persistent reference workflows · MCPCN</title><meta name="description" content="React components and workflow blocks for human-controlled MCP Apps."/><link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg?icon.0-2l4nus4v8l3.svg" sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml"/><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/0c0hxoamwjsbw.js" noModule=""></script></head><body><div hidden=""><!--$--><!--/$--></div><header class="site-nav"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">M</span>MCPCN</a><nav><a href="/docs">Docs</a><a href="/components">Components</a><a href="/blocks">Blocks</a><a href="/examples">Examples</a><a href="/playground">Playground</a></nav><div class="nav-actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/create">Create</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui" class="button">GitHub</a></div></header><main class="docs-layout server-guide"><aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Reference workflow guide"><a href="/docs">Documentation</a><a href="/examples">Five reference apps</a><a href="#run">Run locally</a><a href="#review">Review and confirm</a><a href="#boundaries">Access and data boundaries</a></aside><article class="prose" style="min-width:0" aria-label="Persistent reference workflow guide"><span class="eyebrow">Working examples</span><h1>Review a real change. Keep its audit.</h1><p>Five reference applications connect React review surfaces to actual MCP tools and a persistent private SQLite workspace. Inspect supplied evidence,correct fields,review an order,change a reference preference or save a research decision.</p><h2 id="run">Run locally</h2><p>Use Node 24.22.2 and pnpm 10.24.0 on macOS or Linux. Clone the repository,or <a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/releases/download/v0.1.0-reference-workflows.1/mcpcn-reference-workbench-0.1.0.tgz">download the focused workbench source</a> and extract it. From its root:</p><pre class="code" aria-label="Reference workbench commands">pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts
pnpm examples:build
pnpm examples:dev --workspace /absolute/private/reference-workspace</pre><p>Choose an empty private directory or a recognized reference workspace you own. Open the printed loopback address and enter the per-launch access code. Keep the listener local and the code private. Press Ctrl-C to close it; use the same workspace path to reopen saved records and audit events.</p><h2 id="review">Review and confirm</h2><ol><li>Open a server record and inspect its complete supplied data.</li><li>Propose a decision or correction. The server prepares exact terms against the current revision.</li><li>Review the before/after values and check a fresh acknowledgement. Confirmation persists the change and its audit atomically.</li><li>Reload the record to verify its actual saved state. Cancelled,expired or stale reviews cannot apply a change.</li></ol><p>Checkout records an uncharged local order,with server-owned prices,shipping,tax,return terms and a reviewed quote-refresh path. Settings rollback also requires a fresh review. Document extraction accepts explicitly submitted UTF-8 invoice,contract or resume text; its literal-line matches are not OCR or a model interpretation. Research gathers configured primary sources,retains partial failures,retries only the selected failed source and saves your own final decision.</p><h2 id="boundaries">Access and data boundaries</h2><p>The workbench uses real Client/McpServer and official AppBridge/OfficialMCPAdapter traffic. It derives a trusted local principal from the selected private workspace and OS operator. Host/Origin checks,a per-launch capability and a short-lived HttpOnly SameSite cookie protect local requests. It serves trusted built-in apps; its iframe is not a sandbox for arbitrary third-party HTML.</p><p>Only deliberate identifiers,status and receipts are model-visible. Full source text,addresses,notes and prepared tokens use explicit app metadata,which remains visible to the host. Metadata,visibility and a consent checkbox do not authenticate a user or prove human identity. Public or multi-user deployments must supply verified transport authentication.</p><p>No card is charged,no candidate is contacted,and no SSO,email,OCR or AI provider is configured. These are persistent local reference workflows. Production identity/providers,external-host compatibility,Windows and full accessibility/device acceptance remain separate. A failed network response can follow a completed mutation: reload and inspect the saved audit before trying another action.</p><p><a href="/examples">Browse the five applications</a>,read their <a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/tree/main/examples">source and runbook</a>,or <a href="/docs/server">build your own validated MCP server</a>. Block server recipes are a separate dependent library deliverable.</p></article></main><!--$--><!--/$--><footer><div><strong>MCPCN</strong><p>Human control for agentic apps.</p></div><div><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui">GitHub</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Security</a></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ddg70z30qn04.js" id="_R_" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[14058,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"\"]\n3:I[43820,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\"]\n4:I[98737,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\"]\n14:I[98025,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\",1]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3lg58otdl8my-.css\",\"style\"]\n12:X\n0:{\"P\":null,\"c\":[\"\",\"docs\",\"reference-workflows\"],\"q\":\"\",\"i\":false,\"f\":[[[\"\",{\"children\":[\"docs\",{\"children\":[\"reference-workflows\",{\"children\":[\"__PAGE__\",{},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4608]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4608]},\"$unde